{
  // Typecheck for the standalone harnesses under `tests/`. The main tsconfig
  // cannot cover them: it pins `rootDir: "src"` and `include: ["src"]`, so
  // everything here is outside the build by construction — the `exclude`
  // entry for `tests` was belt-and-braces, not the cause.
  //
  // Why this exists: `tests/security/exfil-injection` calls into the real
  // network guard. Without a typecheck, a signature change in core leaves the
  // harness calling the old shape, it throws at runtime, and its catch turns
  // that into the "blocked" result — the security suite then reports a clean
  // run while measuring nothing.
  //
  // Scoped to `tests/security` deliberately. The rest of `tests/` carries 17
  // pre-existing errors across 9 files (measured 2026-08-23); widening is a
  // separate change and must not ride along in a security fix.
  //
  // `include` names only `tests/security`: tsc pulls the imported `src` files
  // in as dependencies and checks them, so a wrong-arity call into the guard
  // is caught without re-checking all of src a second time (2.6s vs 2.9s).
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "incremental": false
  },
  "include": ["tests/security", "tests/contract-env.test.ts",
    // The probe-freshness pair, so `probe-freshness.d.mts` binds SOMEWHERE. Before this,
    // `tests/eval` was in no tsc project and the declaration was checked by nothing at all.
    //
    // What this does and does not buy, stated because the first version of this comment
    // claimed the stronger thing: it pins the TESTS' CALL SITES against the declaration. It
    // does NOT verify the declaration against the module — `allowJs` is off, so tsc never
    // loads `probe-freshness.mjs`, and a ghost export or a wrong return type there still
    // compiles clean. The module-vs-declaration drift is caught by the runtime tests, not
    // by tsc.
    //
    // Only these two files, not the whole directory — the rest of `tests/eval` was never in
    // a project and dragging it in is a different job.
    "tests/eval/probe-freshness.test.ts",
    "tests/eval/probe-freshness-members.test.ts"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
